<title>PHILIPPINES: C&amp;P Homes Q1 net sharply up.</title>
<headline>C&amp;P Homes Q1 net sharply up.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>C&amp;P Homes Inc, the largest housing developer in the Philippines, reported on Wednesday a net income of 659 million pesos in the first quarter, compared with 548 million in the year-earlier period.  </p>
<p>Net sales in the first three months reached 2.04 billion pesos, against 1.70 billion in the same period last year.</p>
<p>&quot;The company benefited from the strong demand for affordable housing,&quot; said Manuel Villar, company chairman and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>The firm sold 5,368 housing units in the first quarter, up from 4,968 last year.</p>
<p>-- MANILA NEWSROOM (63 2) 841-8939</p>
</text>
